<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Michael Panaretos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1320–after 1390</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Michael Panaretos was a Greek official and historian of the Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trebizond</a> in the fourteenth century, who served Emperor Alexios III at court and on embassies. His short chronicle, covering the empire from its foundation in 1204 to about 1390, is the only surviving native history of Trebizond and the main source for its court and civil wars.</p></div>
